Name: quic_retry
Type: ENUM
Allowed-Values: never load always
Default-Value: load
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

When master answers a new QUIC connection with a Retry packet, to make the
client prove it can receive at its source address before a worker is given
to it (RFC 9000 section 8.1).  This keeps a flood of Initial packets with
forged source addresses from tying up workers, at the cost of one round trip
on each connection it applies to.

"load" sends a Retry only while the service has at least half of its maxchild
workers running, so a service without a maxchild limit never sends one.
"always" sends a Retry for every new connection, and "never" for none.
